  "not_a_relitigation_of_sc29": true,
  "sc29_distinction": "SC29 asked whether a probe trained on a lung atlas (GSE130148) flags liver parenchyma (hepatocyte, cholangiocyte) as novel across atlases; it was killed (novel-type AUROC 0.425, CI [0.394, 0.463]). SC32 does not re-open that cross-atlas question. SC32 trains and tests inside MacParland liver only: a probe fit on remaining liver types in training donors is asked to flag a held-out liver type in a held test donor. A within-atlas survive here would not reverse the SC29 kill; a within-atlas fail would not be blamed on the SC29 protocol confound.",
  "sc29_dest": "${SOURCE_ROOT}/Desktop/singlecell-genomics-research/research/results/SC29/sc29_macparland_liver_vs_gse130148.json",
  "sc29_dest_sha256": "3b2182d55921d724be6c1bf196ee76f9c870b40f07b02aa80ca14bfa1c0e7282",
  "preregistration_note": "Full MacParland liver type list with n_total>=60 is frozen here before any novelty AUROC is computed. This replicates a protocol fixed on GSE130148 (SC31): donor-held-out splits, HVG(1000)+PCA(30)+logistic, temperature on a held calibration donor, novelty score = 1-max softmax, n_boot=200, min_n_total=60, min_n_held=30. Types with n_in_held_donor<30 are listed as underpowered and excluded from the aggregate; no alternate donor fold is fabricated to rescue them. Types are not coarsened.",
  "split_rule_count_only": "held = donor maximizing n of (n_total>=60 types with n_held>=30); ties broken by larger donor n; cal = largest remaining donor; train = the rest. Rule uses type x donor counts only, never AUROC. The largest donor C41_P3TLH is 83% hepatocyte and would leave innate lymphoid cell at n_held=0 (plus several other eligible types underpowered), so it is used as calibration rather than test. This is one global split, not a per-type fold, and is not SC29's largest-donor query split.",
  "metric_preregistered": "per-type AUROC of (1-max softmax) on held-donor remaining types vs held-donor cells of the removed type; bootstrap 95% CI n_boot=200; label-shuffle null; acc@80cov vs forced on the mixed held-donor test set",
  "split": "donor-held-out donor_id; train=['C37_P1TLH', 'C39_P2TLH', 'C42_P4TLH']; cal=C41_P3TLH; test=C43_P5TLH; temperature on cal donor only; never random cells",
  "features": "HVG(1000)+PCA(30)+logistic; fit on remaining types in train donors only",
  "novelty_score": "1 - max_softmax after temperature scaling",
